      "side": 1,
      "message": "As you can see from HFP spec, CVSD codec is Madatory codec.\nSo remote device should support CVSD codec.\n\nAnd p_scb-\u003epeer_codecs\u0027s initial value is BTM_SCO_CODEC_CVSD.\nOnly when HF does not send CVSD (1) using BAC (Spec out), p_scb-\u003epeer_codecs\u0027s is set without BTM_SCO_CODEC_CVSD.\n\nAlthough \"p_scb-\u003epeer_codecs \u0026 BTM_SCO_CODEC_CVSD\" condition is false, \"BTA_AgSetCodec(bta_ag_scb_to_idx(p_scb), BTM_SCO_CODEC_CVSD);\" should be called.\nBecause SCO is opened with CVSD settings.\n\nSince SCO will be opened, we should select any codec.\nSince HF requested Audio connection by HCI_Connection_Request, no other codec (mSBC, LC3) can be selected, and we have no choice but to select the default codec, CVSD.\n\nSo, if you want to add log for that case, below is better.\n\n```suggestion\n      if (p_scb-\u003epeer_codecs \u0026 BTM_SCO_CODEC_CVSD) {\n        log::error(\"CVSD codec is not supported, but set CVSD codec by default\");\n      }\n      BTA_AgSetCodec(bta_ag_scb_to_idx(p_scb), BTM_SCO_CODEC_CVSD);\n```",
      "parentUuid": "ce7cef47_b760d8dd",
      "revId": "537169fbe321a9845434044a2479b35b11e247b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
